    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d298">

                <pb facs="0431" n="346" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg346"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/872: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bailly-Blanchard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-20T12:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 20,
                                1919, 12 noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            8.10 p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Department’s September 18, 4 p.m.<anchor n="43" xml:id="d298-f1"/> Full powers
                    not yet received. McIlhenny will leave immediately after signature protocol.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Blanchard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d298-f1" n="43" xml:id="d298-f1-content">
                <p>“Cable Department whether protocol has been signed and when McIlhenny will
                    leave.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
